wifi: wcn36xx: retry DELETE_BSS and drop the handle when it fails

The firmware has WCN36XX_HAL_NUM_BSSID (2) BSS slots and an AP+STA
build uses both, so the station's BSS index is the only slot it can
ever have.  When DELETE_BSS is refused, wcn36xx keeps that index, and
everything that follows reuses a handle the firmware no longer agrees
with:

    phy0-sta0: disassociated (Reason: 15=4WAY_HANDSHAKE_TIMEOUT)
    wcn36xx: ERROR hal_delete_bss response failed err=5
    wcn36xx: ERROR hal_remove_bsskey response failed err=16
    wcn36xx: ERROR hal_delete_sta_self response failed err=7

Status 5 is WCN36XX_FW_MSG_RESULT_MEM_FAIL, so the refusal may be
transient; retry once before giving up.  If the second attempt fails
too, drop the index anyway.  A DELETE_BSS the firmware did not
acknowledge leaves an index that cannot be trusted, reusing it only
produces the further bogus statuses above, and the next CONFIG_BSS
allocates a fresh slot from the response.

Measured on MSM8916 with concurrent AP+STA, 2026-11-05: after a local
deauth (a LuCI channel-width change on the AP vif) the firmware
answered status 5 for every reconnect, 29 times over 9 minutes, and
the station associated each time but never completed the 4-way
handshake.  Only a driver reload cleared it.  This patch stops the
cascade and gives the transient case a second chance; the reload
itself is handled by the wifi-sta-up watchdog, which now escalates on
repeated handshake timeouts instead of walking the supplicant-restart
ladder.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/smd.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/smd.c
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include <linux/etherdevice.h>
 #include <linux/firmware.h>
 #include <linux/bitops.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/rpmsg.h>
 #include "smd.h"
 #include "firmware.h"
@@ -1910,36 +1911,61 @@
 	return ret;
 }
 
+#define WCN36XX_DELETE_BSS_TRIES	2
+
 int wcn36xx_smd_delete_bss(struct wcn36xx *wcn, struct ieee80211_vif *vif)
 {
 	struct wcn36xx_hal_delete_bss_req_msg msg_body;
 	struct wcn36xx_vif *vif_priv = wcn36xx_vif_to_priv(vif);
-	int ret = 0;
+	int ret = 0, i;
 
 	mutex_lock(&wcn->hal_mutex);
 
 	if (vif_priv->bss_index == WCN36XX_HAL_BSS_INVALID_IDX)
 		goto out;
 
-	INIT_HAL_MSG(msg_body, WCN36XX_HAL_DELETE_BSS_REQ);
+	/*
+	 * The firmware has WCN36XX_HAL_NUM_BSSID (2) BSS slots and an AP+STA
+	 * setup uses both, so a refused DELETE_BSS leaves the station's only
+	 * slot holding its old key: the next CONFIG_BSS reuses that slot, the
+	 * new key cannot be installed, and the 4-way handshake times out.  The
+	 * station then associates but never carries data, and only a driver
+	 * reload clears it (observed 2026-11-05: status 5 on every reconnect,
+	 * 29 handshake timeouts over 9 minutes).
+	 *
+	 * Status 5 is MEM_FAIL, so the failure may be transient.  Retry once;
+	 * if it still fails the handle is dropped anyway.  A DELETE_BSS that
+	 * the firmware did not acknowledge leaves an index we cannot trust, and
+	 * reusing it only produces more bogus statuses (16 on RMV_BSSKEY, 7 on
+	 * DEL_STA_SELF) while the next CONFIG_BSS allocates a fresh slot.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < WCN36XX_DELETE_BSS_TRIES; i++) {
+		INIT_HAL_MSG(msg_body, WCN36XX_HAL_DELETE_BSS_REQ);
 
-	msg_body.bss_index = vif_priv->bss_index;
+		msg_body.bss_index = vif_priv->bss_index;
 
-	PREPARE_HAL_BUF(wcn->hal_buf, msg_body);
+		PREPARE_HAL_BUF(wcn->hal_buf, msg_body);
 
-	wcn36xx_dbg(WCN36XX_DBG_HAL, "hal delete bss %d\n", msg_body.bss_index);
+		wcn36xx_dbg(WCN36XX_DBG_HAL, "hal delete bss %d (try %d)\n",
+			    msg_body.bss_index, i + 1);
 
-	ret = wcn36xx_smd_send_and_wait(wcn, msg_body.header.len);
-	if (ret) {
-		wcn36xx_err("Sending hal_delete_bss failed\n");
-		goto out;
-	}
-	ret = wcn36xx_smd_rsp_status_check(wcn->hal_buf, wcn->hal_rsp_len);
-	if (ret) {
-		wcn36xx_err("hal_delete_bss response failed err=%d\n", ret);
-		goto out;
+		ret = wcn36xx_smd_send_and_wait(wcn, msg_body.header.len);
+		if (ret) {
+			wcn36xx_err("Sending hal_delete_bss failed\n");
+			goto out;
+		}
+		ret = wcn36xx_smd_rsp_status_check(wcn->hal_buf, wcn->hal_rsp_len);
+		if (!ret)
+			break;
+
+		if (i + 1 < WCN36XX_DELETE_BSS_TRIES)
+			msleep(20);
 	}
 
+	if (ret)
+		wcn36xx_warn("hal_delete_bss %d failed err=%d; dropping the handle\n",
+			     vif_priv->bss_index, ret);
+
 	vif_priv->bss_index = WCN36XX_HAL_BSS_INVALID_IDX;
 out:
 	mutex_unlock(&wcn->hal_mutex);
